abstract: >-
  Software accompanying Nishioka et al. (2025, Frontiers in Materials,
  doi:10.3389/fmats.2025.1652484). Implements a defect localization
  pipeline for perforated carbon-fiber-reinforced plastic (CFRP)
  interstage structures combining finite element method (FEM) stress
  simulation with a graph attention network (GAT) classifier. Surface
  stress distributions extracted from FEM serve as node features on a
  graph representing the specimen geometry; the GAT predicts defect
  position from 19 depth-and-location categories. Achieves macro-F1
  of 61% with accurate joint prediction of insertion depth and planar
  location. Developed in collaboration with JAXA for structural health
  monitoring of H3 rocket CFRP fairing components.

